The "Full Duplex" BIOS Setting Is Not Audio

"Duplex Select" in BIOS controls the transmission mode of the IR (Infra-Red) communications port, not the audio subsystem. Full-Duplex permits simultaneous two-way transmission. Half-Duplex only permits transmission in one direction at a time.

The Duplex Select BIOS feature is found under Onboard Serial Port 2 — it is slaved to the second serial port, so if that serial port is disabled, this option disappears or appears grayed out.
